coder › Done. Committed as `2f4bef2` on `work/main`.

**What changed in `src/range.ts`:**
- Added `parseInstant(value)` — `Date.parse`s one value and throws `new TypeError(\`unparseable date: ${value}\`)` when the result is `NaN`.
- Added `parseRange(range)` — parses `start` first, then `end`, then throws a `RangeError` if `end < start`.
- `overlaps` now validates `a` first, then `b`, before doing anything else (so invalid input always throws, regardless of the other range). If either range is zero-length (`start === end`) it returns `false`. Otherwise it returns `aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd` — strict `<` on both sides, making touching ranges false and same-start ranges true.

**What `src/range.test.ts` added** (keeping the existing hour-overlap test): touching ranges → `false`; same-start ranges → `true`; zero-length range against a strictly containing range (both argument orders) and against itself → `false`; unparseable start and unparseable end each throw `TypeError` with a message containing the offending value; end before start throws `RangeError`.

